  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 0,
  "section_notes": "S2 was substantially loosened: a 7% permanent cap with a seven-year transition, during which models above 5% can continue to be sold. This mainly benefits Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S1, S4 and S5 remain strong, with a numeric 8 per 100k recall trigger. Customers receive per-model results and the public does not, which satisfies both sides' red lines. The S3 retrofit deadline is six years, with a feasibility qualifier but alternative upgrades required."
